    "title": "Measurement of the top-quark production cross-section and charge asymmetry at LHCb",
    "arxiv": "[hep-ex/2512.11324v1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.11324)",
    "time": "2025.12.12",
    "abstract": "The first measurements of the top- and antitop-quark differential production cross-sections and the top-quark charge asymmetry in the forward region are presented, using proton-proton collision data collected by the LHCb experiment at a centre-of-mass energy of 13 TeV corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 5.4 fb$^{-1}$. The total production cross-sections of top and antitop quarks are also determined. Measurements are performed using the $\\mu+b$-jet final state within a fiducial region defined by a $b$-jet $p_{\\mathrm{T, jet}} > 50$ GeV and pseudorapidity $2.2 < \\eta_{\\mathrm{jet}} < 4.0$, with the muon from the $W$-boson decay required to have $p_{\\mathrm{T},\\mu} > 25$ GeV and pseudorapidity $2.0 < \\eta_\\mu < 4.5$. The muon and $b$-jet system must satisfy $p_{\\mathrm{T}}(\\mu + \\mathrm{jet}) > 20$ GeV. The measured integrated production cross-sections for the top and antitop quarks are $\\sigma_t = 0.95 \\pm 0.04 \\pm 0.08 \\pm 0.02$ pb, $\\sigma_{\\bar{t}} = 0.81 \\pm 0.03 \\pm 0.07 \\pm 0.02$ pb, where the first uncertainty is statistical, the second systematic, and the third accounts for the luminosity uncertainty. The top-quark charge asymmetry is measured to be $A_C^t = 0.08 \\pm 0.03 \\pm 0.01$, where the first uncertainty is statistical and the second is systematic. These results are consistent with next-to-leading-order Standard Model predictions.",
